/* ===== Airport diagrams ready before you open them =====
   An airport's diagram is built by the EFB server from OpenStreetMap the first time anyone asks for it, which can take
   half a minute for a big airport; after that the server keeps it for months. So the EFB asks ahead, quietly, for the
   airports of Polaris's network, the loaded flight plan and the airports saved in Weather: one at a time, a few seconds
   apart, at most once every few weeks per airport on this device. It only knocks (warm=1): the server answers at once
   with a few bytes and builds and keeps the diagram on its own, so nothing big is downloaded. */
